# Configuration for update-m1n1 on Slackware AArch64 / Apple Silicon.
# Installed as /etc/default/update-m1n1.  Sourced by /usr/bin/update-m1n1, which
# assembles <ESP>/m1n1/boot.bin from these inputs.
#
# Nothing runs update-m1n1 during install: a fresh install boots the m1n1
# stage 2, U-Boot and device trees the Asahi installer put on the ESP.  Running
# it replaces all three with the pieces named here.

# m1n1 stage 2 and U-Boot both come from the hwm-bw-mac package, which
# installs them into /usr/lib/asahi-boot/.  update-m1n1 already defaults to
# these paths, so they are left commented for reference.
#M1N1="/usr/lib/asahi-boot/m1n1.bin"
#U_BOOT="/usr/lib/asahi-boot/u-boot-nodtb.bin"

# Device trees: the KERNEL's, from the newest installed -armv8-mac module tree.
# Upstream's Arch package makes the same choice (its update-m1n1 defaults DTBS
# to /lib/modules/<newest>/dtbs/*.dtb, and its pacman hook re-runs it whenever
# those change).
#
# NOT the trees hwm-bw-mac installs under /usr/lib/asahi-boot/dtb.  Those are
# U-Boot's mainline device trees, and they lack nodes Asahi's drivers need: the
# display controller, the sound card and headphone codec, and the M2 laptops'
# keyboard and trackpad.  A boot.bin built from them boots without those.
#
# Unquoted on purpose: update-m1n1 expands the glob itself.
DTBS=$(/bin/ls -d /lib/modules/*-armv8-mac 2>/dev/null | sort -rV | head -1)/dtbs/*.dtb
